talismans-south-park-ontology-explainer:concepts-intro a talismans-south-park-ontology-explainer:PageTexts ;
    erb:key "concepts-intro" ;
    talismans-south-park-ontology-explainer:pageTextId "concepts-intro" ;
    talismans-south-park-ontology-explainer:text "The same ontology as ordinary tables: a table of individuals, a table for each class, and a table or a column for each property. An edit here is written straight to the rows the explainer runs on, as the matching change of its things, properties and statements; nothing is kept twice. What a table is comes from its fields. What its fields cannot say (a label, symmetric, inverse of) is on its row of ERBTables or ERBFields." .

